.Dd September 17, 2026
.Dt CBP 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cbp ,
.Nm bpp
.Nd C Build Program++ (CBP) build system, utility, and library API
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm bpp build
.Op Ar files
.Op Fl -options
.br
.Nm cbp
.Op Ar files
.Nm cbp
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Sy C Build Program++ (CBP)
is a drop-in, plug-and-play 1-file C/C++ build system and command-line toolchain. Unlike traditional build systems (such as CMake or Make), CBP does not require a separate build directory or a custom Domain Specific Language (DSL). Instead, projects are configured entirely in plain C++ using a single `build.cpp` file.
.Sh BUILD PLUS PLUS (BPP)
The
.Nm bpp
utility is the bootstrap and management CLI tool for CBP-related projects.
.Pp
When executed with:
.Dl bpp build Ar files ...
it compiles your `build.cpp` script, generates the project builder executable (`cbp`), and sets up the build environment.
.Sh C BUILD PROGRAM++ (CBP)
The
.Nm cbp
utility is the project-specific builder executable produced after executing
.Ic bpp build .
.Pp
Running:
.Dl cbp Ar files ...
invokes your custom `build_main` routine defined in `build.cpp`, compiles your application source files, links required libraries, and outputs the final binary according to your specifications.
.Sh LIBCBP API
The
.Sy libcbp
library provides namespaces, structures, and helper functions within the
.Li CBuildP
namespace to construct powerful C/C++ build scripts inside `build.cpp`.
.Ss Namespaces and Structures
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Li CBuildP::opt_t
Configuration structure for compiler optimization and debugging settings:
.Bd -literal
struct opt_t {
    const char *compiler = "clang";
    int level = 0;           /* optimization level (0-3) */
    bool debug = true;       /* generate debug symbols */
    static void prints(const opt_t &opt);
};
.Ed
.It Li CBuildP::compilers
Available compiler presets:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Li c::clang , c::gcc
C compilers (`"clang"`, `"gcc"`)
.It Li cpp::clang , cpp::gcc , cxx::clang , cxx::gcc
C++ compilers (`"clang++"`, `"g++"`)
.El
.It Li CBuildP::optimization
Optimization level constants and aliases:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Li none (0)
No optimization
.It Li level1 (1) , fast (1)
Basic optimization (`-O1`)
.It Li level2 (2)
Intermediate optimization (`-O2`)
.It Li level3 (3) , max (3)
Maximum optimization (`-O3`)
.El
.It Li CBuildP::libtype
Library output format constants:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Li STATIC
Static library format (`.a`)
.It Li SHARED
Shared library format (`.so`)
.El
.El
.Ss Functions
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fn CBuildP::get_files "int argc" "char *argv[]"
Extracts and validates input C/C++ source files from command-line arguments.
.It Fn CBuildP::specs "const file_t &file_names" "const file_t &out_file"
Prints build specifications including source files, output binary name, optimization level, debug mode, and compiler.
.It Fn CBuildP::optimize "const opt_t &opt"
Sets and displays compiler optimization level and debug flag settings with animated feedback.
.It Fn CBuildP::include "const std::vector<file_t> &dirs"
Adds include directories (`-Ipath`) for compilation flags.
.It Fn CBuildP::link "const std::vector<file_t> &libraries" "const std::vector<file_t> &look_for_dirs"
Links external libraries (`-l`) searching specified directory paths (`-L`).
.It Fn CBuildP::compile_flags "const std::vector<file_t> &flags"
Appends custom raw compilation flags (such as `-pthread`).
.It Fn CBuildP::compile_link "const std::vector<std::string> &link_cmd_comp"
Appends custom raw linker commands or flags.
.It Fn CBuildP::compile "const file_t &file_names" "const file_t &outfile"
Compiles the specified source files with current flags, optimization, and linkage, producing the final executable.
.It Fn CBuildP::compile_lib "const std::vector<file_t> &file_names" "const file_t &libname" "const file_t &dir" "const std::vector<file_t> &libtypes" "const bool &clean"
Compiles source files into object files and archives them into a static library (`.a`).
.It Fn CBuildP::execcmd "const std::string &cmd"
Executes a shell command via `popen` and returns its output as a `std::string` (useful for integrating tools like `pkg-config`).
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
A basic `build.cpp` script using `libcbp`:
.Bd -literal
#include "vendor/cbp/src/cbp.hpp"

void build_main(int argc, char** argv) {
    CBuildP::file_t input_files = CBuildP::get_files(argc, argv);
    CBuildP::file_t output_file = "bin/my_program";

    CBuildP::optimize({
        .compiler = CBuildP::compilers::cxx::clang,
        .level = CBuildP::optimization::max,
        .debug = true
    });
    CBuildP::specs(input_files, output_file);
    CBuildP::compile(input_files, output_file);
}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr make 1 ,
.Xr cmake 1
